 "final_text": "`/work/combi_hackmath_4.lean` now compiles with no errors and no `sorry` warning. The only output left is a deprecation warning for `push_neg`, which I left alone.\n\nThe proof is by pigeonhole in both directions:\n- **13 is enough:** if some `f : Fin 13 \u2192 Fin 12` had no two equal values, it would be injective. That would force 13 \u2264 12 by `Fintype.card_le_of_injective`, a contradiction.\n- **Nothing smaller works:** if `n < 13`, the map sending `i` to its own value in `Fin 12` has no repeated values. That contradicts the assumption that every `f` has a collision.\n\nI replaced only the `sorry`; the imports, statement and `hackmath_4_solution` are unchanged.",
